# Why this file exists.
#
# `gcloud run deploy --source .` has no .gcloudignore of its own to read, so it silently falls
# back to .gitignore. .gitignore excludes `web/dist/` — correct, it is a build artifact — but
# web/dist is the ONE thing the Dockerfile needs (`COPY web/dist /usr/share/nginx/html`). The
# build context therefore arrived without it and `COPY` failed with a bare "exit status 1".
# Every tool behaved correctly; the combination did not. This file breaks that fallback.
#
# It is also an allowlist, not a blocklist. The container is nginx over static files, so the
# build context needs exactly three things. Shipping src/, test/, docs/, node_modules/ and .git
# to Cloud Build achieves nothing except a slower build and a larger attack surface.
#
# Run `bun run build` before deploying — this file uploads web/dist, it does not create it.

# Ignore everything...
*

# ...except what the Dockerfile actually reads.
!Dockerfile
!nginx.conf

# `!web/` is needed to descend into the directory at all, but on its own it also re-includes
# web/'s other children (preview.html, tsconfig.json, .DS_Store). Re-ignore them, then carve
# dist back out. Order matters: gitignore semantics apply last-match-wins, per path depth.
!web/
web/*
!web/dist/
!web/dist/**
